+`government/economy-models.py` now retains every explicitly configured model
+across catalogue omissions, failed probes, temporary exclusions and size
+limits; validates a temporary candidate rather than writing/restoring live
+config; serializes live writes with a lock and refuses a concurrent config
+change. Its noncanonical refresh guard prevents test worktrees from probing or
+rewriting production state. I ran the canonical non-destructive command
+`python3 government/economy-models.py refresh --no-apply --probe-limit 0` at
+17:52Z: exit 0, `changed=false`, `free_available_now=4`, `funding_risk=none`.
+The live configured list was not changed and no probe ran.
+
+The 17:52Z quota report shows the nine exact OpenCode models in the Act34
+zero-billed policy cooling until approximately 2026-11-25 00:53Z. The four
+currently eligible general free routes are `opencode-go/beam-free`,
+`opencode-go/hy4-flash-free`, `opencode-go/hungerg-free`, and
+`opencode-go/iceman-contributor-free`. Thus the current Act34 allowlist has no
